{
 "_doc": {
  "owner": "check_g5_skin.py (T20). Production scripts read only.",
  "format": "poses[]: id, group (sheet: shoulder/elbow/wrist/hip/knee/ankle/spine_head/full), side (l/r/c), tier (judged/report), joint (joint name, list of joint names, or 'all' = every limb joint both sides), rot {bone: [X, Y, Z] local Euler degrees, rotation_mode XYZ (Blender: X applied first, all about the bone's rest frame)}, kind + col (sheet row/column labels; limb col = signed pose angle), view (cell render view). Bones not listed stay at rest. Twist bones (upperarm_twist_x, lowerarm_twist_x) are never listed: their constraints drive them.",
  "sign_derivation": "From canonical_skeleton.json rest_matrix columns (X, Y = bone axis, Z). Rotating the bone by +a about local axis A moves its tail along A x Y (right hand rule). Arm L: X=(-0.028,+0.202,-0.979)~-Z, Y~+X, Z=(+0.037,-0.978,-0.203)~-Y. Arm R: X=(-0.029,-0.176,+0.984)~+Z, Y~-X, Z=(-0.042,-0.983,-0.177)~-Y. => +X: X x Y = +Z_local ~ -Y world, arm/forearm/hand moves forward (-Y) on both sides (G4.4: lowerarm +X -> hand -Y). +Z: Z x Y = -X_local: L -> +Z world (raise), R -> -Z world (lower); so shoulder raise = upperarm_l Z +a, upperarm_r Z -a. Shoulder forward = upperarm X +a, back = X -a. Leg L/R (thigh, calf): X~+X, Y~-Z, Z~+Y. +X: tail moves +Z_local ~ +Y (back) (G4.4: calf +X -> foot +Y) => knee flexion = calf X +a, hip flexion (foot forward -Y) = thigh X -a, extension = X +a. +Z: tail moves -X_local ~ -X world: thigh_l Z -a and thigh_r Z +a = abduction (foot outward). Foot L/R: X~(+0.91,+-0.4,..), Y ~ toward foot_tip (-Y), Z~-Z. +X: toe moves -Z => ankle dorsiflexion (toe up, the G3 ankle_30 direction) = foot X -a, plantarflexion = X +a. Spine_01/spine_02/head: X=+X, Y=+Z, Z=-Y. +X: top moves -Y => forward bend = X +a, back = X -a. +Z: top moves -X => bend to the character right (side_r) = Z +a, side_l = Z -a. +Y twist turns the front (-Y) toward +X (character left). Twist poses: upperarm / hand local Y +-a (bone axis).",
  "labels": "shoulder_raise a: arm up by a from T-pose. shoulder_fwd a>0 forward, a<0 back. hip_flex a>0 flexion, a<0 extension. ankle a>0 dorsiflexion (toe up), a<0 plantarflexion. wrist_bend a: hand X +a (a>0 hand toward -Y). ids use 'm' for a minus sign.",
  "tier": "judged = poses carried over from G3 (plan Phase 5 main decision 2026-09-25): shoulder raise/forward 30 and 60, elbow 30 and 60, knee 30 and 60, hip flexion 30 and 60 (not extension), wrist twist +90 (hand local +Y, the G3 wrist_twist_90), ankle 30 (dorsiflexion, the G3 ankle_30). Everything else is report (visual judgement; thresholds fixed by main after first measurement).",
  "ranges": "spec section 4, per side: shoulder raise 0-170 (30/60/90/130/170), shoulder forward/back (30/60/90, -45/-90), upperarm twist +-90, elbow 0-140 (30/60/90/140), wrist twist +-90, wrist bend +-60, hip flexion +-60 (30/60/-30/-60), hip abduction 30/45, knee 0-130 (30/60/90/130), ankle +-30; spine_01/spine_02 bend forward/back/side 30, head bend forward/back/side 30; representative full-body poses: swing windup/impact, walk contact/passing, run max stride, hit lean back, death fall forward, jump crouch. Shoulder raise rotates upperarm only (shoulder bone at rest), same as G3."
 },
